  "notes": "Covenants reflect Amendment No. 6 (Apr 16, 2026); Amendments No. 7 and 8 did not change the financial covenants. Leverage Ratio: during the Covenant Relief Period (Nov 7, 2023 to the earlier of Dec 31, 2028 or the borrower's election to terminate, which requires leverage <=3.75x and interest coverage >=3.50x) the step table applies; afterward the base 3.75x (and 3.50x interest coverage) levels apply, so the 2029-03-31 dates assume the relief period runs to Dec 31, 2028. Amendment 6 waived the Q1 2026 leverage test, and the Leverage Ratio is not tested for the quarters ending Mar 31, Jun 30 and Sep 30, 2026; interest coverage is still tested in those quarters. Both leverage ratios net only unrestricted cash above a $150M floor; this is a floor, not a cap, and escrowed debt proceeds count as unrestricted cash. EBITDA adds back all non-cash charges (which covers stock comp), Non-Recurring Items (restructuring provisions, discontinued operations, special reserves, asset write-downs/write-offs), and M&A/divestiture fees, plus up to $100M of non-recurring cash restructuring charges during the relief period. It also gives pro forma credit for acquisitions. There are no cost-savings or synergy add-backs. Amendment 6 converted the facility to a secured, guaranteed structure (Guarantee and Collateral Agreement, subsidiary guarantors in Eligible Jurisdictions, intercompany subordination) and added the Secured Leverage covenant. It also permits pari passu secured debt on the Collateral subject to covenant compliance, and a First Lien Pari Passu Intercreditor Agreement dated June 5, 2026 exists with U.S. Bank as Additional First Lien Agent. Relief-period restrictions: dividends capped at $0.08/quarter unless pro forma leverage <=3.75x; buybacks limited; non-guarantor subsidiary debt capped at $350M. Amendment 7 permits a first-priority lien on the Rimisoxafen ('Rimi IP') in favor of Corteva securing up to $200M of refund obligations, released the lenders' lien on that IP, and requires re-grant when the Corteva lien ends. Amendment 8 waived missed joinder deadlines (New US LLC guarantor joinder; New Dutch BV intercompany subordination joinder). It also released liens on FMC India equity, contributed cash (<=$25M), cancelled receivables and intercompany claims, and releases two guarantors at the closing of the FMC India sale, with reinstatement if the sale does not close by Dec 31, 2026. Sale proceeds must go to repaying debt under the facility or to general corporate purposes. Events of default include a Change of Control.",
